  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A number MMM is said to be a Mystical Number with respect to a number XXX if (M⊕X)&gt;(M&amp;X)(M \\oplus X) \\gt (M \\&amp; X)(M⊕X)&gt;(M&amp;X).\n\nYou are given an array AAA of size NNN. You are also given QQQ queries. Each query consists of three integers LLL, RRR, and XXX.\n\nFor each query, find the count of Mystical Numbers in the subarray A[L:R]A[L:R]A[L:R] with respect to the number XXX.\n\n**Notes:**\n\n\n⊕\\oplus⊕ represents the Bitwise XOR operation and &amp;\\&amp;&amp; represents the Bitwise AND operation.\nA[L:R]A[L:R]A[L:R] denotes the subarray A[L],A[L+1],…,A[R]A[L], A[L+1], \\ldots, A[R]A[L],A[L+1],…,A[R].\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT - the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN - the size of the array AAA.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\dots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ denoting the array AAA.\nThe third line of each test case contains&nbsp;an integer&nbsp;QQQ -&nbsp;denoting the number of queries.\nThe ithi^{th}ith of the next QQQ lines contains three space-separated integers LLL , RRR and XXX.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each testcase,\n\n\n\nFor each query, print in a new line, the count of Mystical Numbers among A[L],A[L+1],…,A[R]A[L], A[L+1], \\ldots, A[R]A[L],A[L+1],…,A[R] with respect to the number XXX.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai&lt;2310 \\leq A_i \\lt 2^{31}0≤Ai​&lt;231",
      "1≤Q≤2⋅1051 \\leq Q \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^51≤Q≤2⋅105",
      "1≤L≤R≤N1 \\leq L \\leq R \\leq N1≤L≤R≤N",
      "0≤X&lt;2310 \\leq X \\lt 2^{31}0≤X&lt;231",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105.",
      "Sum of QQQ over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
